{"name":"Straw Hat","hex":"#f0d5a8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"straw hat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stiff hat, made from woven straw."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straw_hat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Straw hat","blocks":[{"text":"A straw hat is a wide-brimmed hat that is woven out of straw or straw-like synthetic materials. Straw hats are a type of sun hat designed to shade the head and face from direct sunlight, but are also used in fashion as a decorative element or a uniform."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Silent_film_comic_Charley_Chase_%28SAYRE_21396%29.jpg/330px-Silent_film_comic_Charley_Chase_%28SAYRE_21396%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straw_hat"},{"title":"Straw Hat (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Straw Hat is a 1971 Czechoslovak comedy film written by Miloš Macourek and Oldřich Lipský, and directed by Lipský as well. It stars Miloš Kopecký in the leading role. The film is based on the 1851 play The Italian Straw Hat by Eugène Labiche and Marc-Michel."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7a/Straw_Hat%2C_Czechoslovak_film_1971%2C_DVD_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straw_Hat_(film)"},{"title":"Straw","blocks":[{"text":"Straw is an agricultural byproduct consisting of the dry stalks of cereal plants after the grain and chaff have been removed. It makes up about half of the yield by weight of cereal crops such as barley, oats, rice, rye and wheat. It has a number of different uses, including fuel, livestock bedding and fodder, thatching and basket making."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Rice_straw.jpg/330px-Rice_straw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straw"},{"title":"Hat","blocks":[{"text":"A hat is a head covering which is worn for various reasons, including protection against weather conditions, ceremonial reasons such as university graduation, religious reasons, comedy, safety, or as a fashion accessory. Hats which incorporate mechanical features, such as visors, spikes, flaps, braces or beer holders shade into the broader category of headgear."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Chapeaux_en_peau_de_castor.jpg/330px-Chapeaux_en_peau_de_castor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hat"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%8C.JPG/500px-%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%8C.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%8C.JPG/1280px-%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%8C.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%8C.JPG/500px-%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%8C.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A traditional Ukrainian straw hat.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%8C.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Ur_AB_Nordiska_Kompaniets_varukatalog%2C